-- title:
--   Anchored Γ₀(M')-equivariance of the Igusa charts
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q \ge 5$, a natural number $M' \ne 0$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ (i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$). Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, let `hle` embed the base-changed full-level field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ into $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, and let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of the former along $A$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$, assumed to reduce coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element lies in $R_0$'s integers and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Fix an index $\zeta$ of primitive $q$-th roots of unity, a family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of valuation subrings of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ indexed by $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q) =$ [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21), and a family $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ indexed by $W$. The hypotheses on $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ are: $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ consists of those $f$ for which there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f \cdot y = x$; every $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}(\gamma) \cdot \infty$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\infty)$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$; $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ is injective; and pullback along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$, for any index $\zeta'$ and any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, permutes the family. Four further hypotheses on $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ (contraction to $A$ on constants, compatibility with the $R_0$-residue at the places of $W$ for functions integral wherever $j$ is, invariance under all $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, and existence of a parameter $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t - a$ a unit for all $a \in A$) are summarised here. Finally let $\mathcal C$ be a semistable covering for $q, M', A, W$ with $(\mathcal C.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell)$'s integers equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ for all $\ell$, satisfying: pullback of $\mathcal C.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ along any $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ has the same domain as $\mathcal C.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ as soon as it has the same integers; for any $\zeta'$, any $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and any permutation $\sigma$ of $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ realising the pullback action on $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$, the annuli satisfy $((\mathcal C.\mathrm{An}\,\ell\,s)\text{ pulled back}).\mathrm{dom} = (\mathcal C.\mathrm{An}\,(\sigma \ell)\,s).\mathrm{dom}$ with equal moduli; and $\mathcal C$ satisfies `EquivClauses`. The conclusion asserts the existence of one index $\zeta_0$ (not necessarily the given $\zeta$) such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\ell$, the pullback of $\mathcal C.\mathrm{CIg}\,\ell$ along $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta_0\,\gamma^{-1}$ has the same integers and the same domain as $\mathcal C.\mathrm{CIg}\,((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1} \cdot \ell)$, and for every $s \in W$ the pullback of $\mathcal C.\mathrm{An}\,\ell\,s$ along the same automorphism has the same domain as $\mathcal C.\mathrm{An}\,((\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1} \cdot \ell)\,s$.
--
--   This is the anchoring step in the construction of the semistable covering of the full-level modular curve: it upgrades the abstract equivariance clauses, which only say that each level automorphism permutes the Igusa components somehow, to the statement that at a single suitable index $\zeta_0$ the permutation is exactly the natural action of $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma)^{-1}$ on $\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$. It is used in the existence theorem [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted), and the two inputs it cites are the composition law `levelAutBar_mul` for level automorphisms on $\Gamma_0(M')$ and the invariance `comap_levelAutBar_eq_of_redQ_smul_lineInfty_eq` of the Gauss ring under automorphisms fixing the line at infinity.
